{"k":"ind","t":"Indefinite Integration","cls":"12","u":"Calculus","s":[["Standard integrals",[{"q":"Power and exponential","f":"\\int x^n\\,dx=\\frac{x^{n+1}}{n+1}+C\\ (n\\ne-1),\\quad\\int\\frac{dx}x=\\ln|x|+C,\\quad\\int e^x\\,dx=e^x+C,\\quad\\int a^x\\,dx=\\frac{a^x}{\\ln a}+C"},{"q":"Trigonometric integrals","f":"\\int\\sin x=-\\cos x,\\ \\int\\cos x=\\sin x,\\ \\int\\sec^2x=\\tan x,\\ \\int\\csc^2x=-\\cot x,\\ \\int\\sec x\\tan x=\\sec x,\\ \\int\\csc x\\cot x=-\\csc x"},{"q":"Integrals of tan, cot, sec, csc","f":"\\int\\tan x\\,dx=\\ln|\\sec x|,\\quad\\int\\cot x\\,dx=\\ln|\\sin x|,\\quad\\int\\sec x\\,dx=\\ln|\\sec x+\\tan x|,\\quad\\int\\csc x\\,dx=\\ln\\left|\\tan\\tfrac x2\\right|","n":"$\\int\\sec x\\,dx=\\ln\\left|\\tan\\left(\\frac\\pi4+\\frac x2\\right)\\right|$; $\\int\\csc x\\,dx=\\ln|\\csc x-\\cot x|$.","d":"$\\int\\sec x\\,dx=\\int\\frac{\\sec x(\\sec x+\\tan x)}{\\sec x+\\tan x}dx$; numerator is the derivative of the denominator."},{"q":"Standard algebraic forms (1)","f":"\\int\\frac{dx}{x^2+a^2}=\\frac1a\\tan^{-1}\\frac xa,\\quad\\int\\frac{dx}{\\sqrt{a^2-x^2}}=\\sin^{-1}\\frac xa","n":"$\\int\\frac{dx}{x\\sqrt{x^2-a^2}}=\\frac1a\\sec^{-1}\\frac xa$."},{"q":"Standard algebraic forms (2)","f":"\\int\\frac{dx}{x^2-a^2}=\\frac1{2a}\\ln\\left|\\frac{x-a}{x+a}\\right|,\\quad\\int\\frac{dx}{a^2-x^2}=\\frac1{2a}\\ln\\left|\\frac{a+x}{a-x}\\right|","d":"Partial fractions: $\\frac1{x^2-a^2}=\\frac1{2a}\\left(\\frac1{x-a}-\\frac1{x+a}\\right)$."},{"q":"Standard algebraic forms (3)","f":"\\int\\frac{dx}{\\sqrt{x^2\\pm a^2}}=\\ln\\left|x+\\sqrt{x^2\\pm a^2}\\right|"},{"q":"Square-root integrals","f":"\\int\\sqrt{a^2-x^2}\\,dx=\\frac x2\\sqrt{a^2-x^2}+\\frac{a^2}2\\sin^{-1}\\frac xa","n":"$\\int\\sqrt{x^2\\pm a^2}\\,dx=\\frac x2\\sqrt{x^2\\pm a^2}\\pm\\frac{a^2}2\\ln\\left|x+\\sqrt{x^2\\pm a^2}\\right|$.","d":"By parts with $u=\\sqrt{a^2-x^2}$, $dv=dx$, then add the integral back to both sides."}]],["Techniques",[{"q":"Integration by parts","f":"\\int u\\,v\\,dx=u\\int v\\,dx-\\int\\left(u'\\int v\\,dx\\right)dx","h":"ILATE: Inverse, Log, Algebraic, Trig, Exponential — choose $u$ from the left."},{"q":"The $e^x$ special form","f":"\\int e^x\\left[f(x)+f'(x)\\right]dx=e^xf(x)+C","n":"Also $\\int\\left[f(x)+xf'(x)\\right]dx=xf(x)+C$."},{"q":"Exponential × trig","f":"\\int e^{ax}\\sin bx\\,dx=\\frac{e^{ax}}{a^2+b^2}(a\\sin bx-b\\cos bx)+C","n":"$\\int e^{ax}\\cos bx\\,dx=\\frac{e^{ax}}{a^2+b^2}(a\\cos bx+b\\sin bx)+C$."},{"q":"Derivative over function","f":"\\int\\frac{f'(x)}{f(x)}dx=\\ln|f(x)|+C,\\qquad\\int\\frac{f'(x)}{\\sqrt{f(x)}}dx=2\\sqrt{f(x)}+C","n":"$\\int[f(x)]^nf'(x)\\,dx=\\frac{[f(x)]^{n+1}}{n+1}+C$."},{"q":"Linear substitution","f":"\\int f(ax+b)\\,dx=\\frac1aF(ax+b)+C"}]],["Standard substitutions",[{"q":"Quadratic in the denominator","f":"\\int\\frac{dx}{ax^2+bx+c}:\\ \\text{complete the square}","n":"$\\int\\frac{px+q}{ax^2+bx+c}dx$: write $px+q=A\\frac d{dx}(ax^2+bx+c)+B$. Same for $\\sqrt{ax^2+bx+c}$."},{"q":"Trig rational: $\\int\\frac{dx}{a+b\\cos x}$","f":"t=\\tan\\tfrac x2:\\ \\ \\cos x=\\frac{1-t^2}{1+t^2},\\ \\sin x=\\frac{2t}{1+t^2},\\ dx=\\frac{2\\,dt}{1+t^2}"},{"q":"$\\int\\frac{dx}{a\\sin^2x+b\\cos^2x+c}$","f":"\\text{divide by } \\cos^2x,\\ \\text{put } t=\\tan x"},{"q":"$\\int\\frac{a\\sin x+b\\cos x}{c\\sin x+d\\cos x}dx$","f":"\\text{Numerator}=A(\\text{Denominator})+B(\\text{Denominator})'"},{"q":"Powers of sin and cos","f":"\\int\\sin^mx\\cos^nx\\,dx:\\ m\\ \\text{odd}\\to t=\\cos x;\\ n\\ \\text{odd}\\to t=\\sin x;\\ m+n\\ \\text{negative even}\\to t=\\tan x"},{"q":"Irrational substitutions","f":"\\int\\frac{dx}{(ax+b)\\sqrt{cx+d}}:\\ t^2=cx+d;\\qquad\\int\\frac{dx}{(px+q)\\sqrt{ax^2+bx+c}}:\\ px+q=\\frac1t","n":"$\\int\\frac{dx}{(ax^2+b)\\sqrt{cx^2+d}}$: $x=\\frac1t$, then $u^2=c+dt^2$."},{"q":"Euler substitutions / trigonometric forms","f":"\\sqrt{a^2-x^2}:\\ x=a\\sin\\theta;\\quad\\sqrt{a^2+x^2}:\\ x=a\\tan\\theta;\\quad\\sqrt{x^2-a^2}:\\ x=a\\sec\\theta","n":"$\\sqrt{\\frac{a-x}{a+x}}$: $x=a\\cos2\\theta$. $\\sqrt{(x-\\alpha)(\\beta-x)}$: $x=\\alpha\\cos^2\\theta+\\beta\\sin^2\\theta$."},{"q":"$\\int\\frac{x^2\\pm1}{x^4+kx^2+1}dx$","f":"\\text{divide by } x^2:\\ \\frac{1\\pm\\frac1{x^2}}{x^2+\\frac1{x^2}+k};\\ \\ t=x\\mp\\frac1x","n":"Used for $\\int\\sqrt{\\tan x}\\,dx$ and $\\int\\frac{dx}{x^4+1}$."}]],["Partial fractions",[{"q":"Partial fraction forms","f":"\\frac{px+q}{(x-a)(x-b)}=\\frac A{x-a}+\\frac B{x-b};\\quad\\frac{\\cdots}{(x-a)^2}=\\frac A{x-a}+\\frac B{(x-a)^2};\\quad\\frac{\\cdots}{(x-a)(x^2+bx+c)}=\\frac A{x-a}+\\frac{Bx+C}{x^2+bx+c}","n":"Cover-up rule for linear factors: $A=\\left.\\frac{px+q}{x-b}\\right|_{x=a}$."}]],["Reduction formulae",[{"q":"Reduction for $\\sin^n x$ and $\\cos^nx$","f":"I_n=\\int\\sin^nx\\,dx=-\\frac{\\sin^{n-1}x\\cos x}n+\\frac{n-1}nI_{n-2}"},{"q":"Reduction for $\\tan^n x$","f":"I_n=\\frac{\\tan^{n-1}x}{n-1}-I_{n-2}"},{"q":"Reduction for $\\sec^n x$","f":"I_n=\\frac{\\sec^{n-2}x\\tan x}{n-1}+\\frac{n-2}{n-1}I_{n-2}"}]],["Common results",[{"q":"Useful results","f":"\\int\\frac{dx}{1+\\sin x}=\\tan x-\\sec x+C,\\qquad\\int\\frac{dx}{1+\\cos x}=\\tan\\frac x2+C","n":"$\\int\\frac{dx}{\\sin x\\cos x}=\\ln|\\tan x|+C$; $\\int\\frac{dx}{\\sin^2x\\cos^2x}=\\tan x-\\cot x+C$."},{"q":"Log integrals","f":"\\int\\ln x\\,dx=x\\ln x-x+C,\\qquad\\int\\frac{\\ln x}x\\,dx=\\frac{(\\ln x)^2}2+C"},{"q":"Inverse trig integrals","f":"\\int\\sin^{-1}x\\,dx=x\\sin^{-1}x+\\sqrt{1-x^2}+C,\\qquad\\int\\tan^{-1}x\\,dx=x\\tan^{-1}x-\\tfrac12\\ln(1+x^2)+C"}]]]}